{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs7CxEegPt2f4CZA8QBz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I implemented `resolver/solve.py` to the spec, and my 8 tests in `tests/test_solve.py` pass. The tests cover:\n- version ordering and hashing\n- constraint parsing\n- the spec's example index\n- a dependency cycle\n- backtracking\n- the error message naming the leaf package\n- unreachable packages being left out\n- a 40-package, 10-version chain that resolves well under 10 seconds\n\nI did not test an index of a few hundred versions, so the 60-second performance requirement is unverified.\n\n**How it picks versions:** it takes the alphabetically first pending package and tries its versions from highest to lowest. It drops a version early if any dependency it adds has no remaining candidate, and it backtracks when a branch dead-ends.\n\n**Preference when the package set varies:** the search always settles the alphabetically first unsettled package, trying its highest version first. For solutions with the same set of packages this gives the lexicographically greatest one. The spec doesn't say how to compare solutions that contain different packages, and the search doesn't compare them. When a choice pulls in a new package, that package is settled afterwards, even if it sorts earlier than ones already chosen.\n\n**Errors:** `ResolutionError` names the package from the deepest dead end, such as `b` in the spec's example. A root requirement that no version satisfies, or a package missing from the index, raises the error naming that package."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12880,"cache_read_input_tokens":26239,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12880},"output_tokens":453,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,